_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The manual says that each line in an abbreviations file must contain one abbreviation without whitespace. It would be convenient if you could use space/tabs but the rest of the line after the first space/tab on were ignored. You could then include expansions and/or comments, making files self-documenting. You could even use a format `abbr. : expansion and/or comment` which would be valid YAML!\r\n\r\nMy use case is that I have a set of Perl scripts which allow me to do certain things with one or more yaml files like described above:\r\n\r\n1.  Search keys and/or values for regex/substring matches.\r\n2.  Generate a (sorted) Markdown table or definition list of abbreviations.\r\n3.  Generate a file containing all unique keys/abbreviations as understood by Pandoc.\r\n\r\nIt would be good to get rid of (3) not because it is a hassle to run the script but because keeping both files updated and in sync is a hassle.\r\n\r\nCf. #8520\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jgm/pandoc/issues/8522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jgm/pandoc/issues/8522/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}